Z||000000||jaguiler||03-14-2001||02:28 PM||||Hi all,<P>I saw a picture of the Fiero GTP that Pontiac made in the eighties to race with.  It was built on a Fiero frame with the same demensions.  Just seems like the fiberglass skin is diffrent.  You would think this would be the easiest kit to make, but I am having trouble finding it... does anyone know anyone that makes one... websites, pictures?<P>Thanks!<P>------------------<BR>______<BR>  |aguiler<BR>\/||209.246.221.174||reg||5
Z||000001||Monkeyman||03-14-2001||02:57 PM||||I'm not positive, but I thought the racing versions were built on a custom tube frame.  Someone let me know if I'm wrong.||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||03-14-2001||08:29 PM||||They were factory sports cars, raced as prototype. tube chassis, lots of different engines were tried. There was a body with spare body parts on ebay about a month ago. It has no parts from or that would fit a factory Fiero. I dont think they build more than 1/2 dozen of them, and just for 2 seasons.||||reg||1
